    ["Using Astropy GM_sun, derive the circular 1-AU period and report the value in days with the conversion steps.", "Integrate the supplied JPL Earth state from Jan 1 to Jan 2 with REBOUND and SciPy. Reconcile the Sun-relative frame, report both residuals in km, and explain why neither residual is a pure solver error.", "For the WHFast sweep, compare relative energy error and endpoint error against timestep. Recommend a step only after naming the quantity and error tolerance you need."],
    ["From the three-body conservation table, calculate the ratio of energy errors between the coarsest and finest timesteps. Does angular momentum show the same trend? Explain with the fixed-step symplectic method.", "Write the equations for the three-body accelerations and identify the smallest dynamical timescale that would control a step-size choice in a close encounter.", "Given a close-encounter interval shorter than the chosen WHFast step, recommend an alternative REBOUND integrator and define two validation criteria before trusting the result."],
    ["Derive the conserved variables and physical flux for one-dimensional ideal-gas Euler flow from mass, momentum, and total-energy conservation.", "Using the generated resolution table, compute successive L1 error ratios and describe whether they support an asymptotic first-order trend. Include the 512-zone reference limitation.", "Audit the Rusanov teaching solver: identify one positivity test, one integral conservation test, one boundary-condition test, and two missing requirements for production astrophysical hydrodynamics."],
    ["Solve dI/dtau=S-I for constant S and boundary I0; show the steps and verify the tau=1 value against the generated record.", "At tau=0.1 and tau=5, compare the first-order thin approximation with the exact solution. State absolute and relative errors and choose a tau domain for a 1% relative-error requirement using a denser computed scan.", "Explain why a grey constant-source slab cannot by itself model a non-LTE scattering atmosphere. Identify which physical terms would change the source function or closure."],
    ["For tau=2, calculate the analytic transmission and compare each seeded N estimate with its standard error. Explain why one seed does not establish a universal confidence interval.", "Derive the likelihood ratio for the tilted Bernoulli proposal and show that its weighted estimator is unbiased. Compare its computed standard error with ordinary sampling at N=10000.", "Fit the synthetic radial-velocity data with the stated model. Report K, phase, gamma, standard errors, weighted chi-square, degrees of freedom, residual RMS, and one residual pattern that would invalidate the model."],
    ["Choose one result from the course and create an audit table separating solver/discretization, stochastic, parameter, measurement, and model uncertainty. Mark inapplicable terms and justify each choice.", "Run the clean-environment command and verify the pinned dependency versions and checksums. Identify one limitation of software-version pinning for random-stream or platform reproducibility.", "Write a 250-word abstract whose conclusion is no stronger than the convergence, residual, and provenance evidence. Attach a reproducibility manifest and one independent cross-check."],
